new file mode 100644
index 00000000..70c8763a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Repository Guidelines
+
+## Project Structure & Module Organization
+- `lib/` contains the core QUIC implementation in C; installed public headers are under `lib/includes/ngtcp2/`.
+- `crypto/` contains backend adapters: `quictls`, `ossl`, `gnutls`, `boringssl`, `wolfssl`, and `picotls`.
+- `tests/` holds Munit-based unit tests (`ngtcp2_*_test.c`) linked into `tests/main`.
+- `examples/` provides client/server programs and simulation code (`sim.cc`, `sim_test.cc`); Python interop tests live in `examples/tests/`.
+- `fuzz/` stores libFuzzer targets and corpora; `doc/source/` contains Sphinx docs; automation lives in `ci/`, `interop/`, and `.github/workflows/`.
+- `third-party/http-parser/` is vendored code; avoid style or behavior changes there unless intentionally syncing upstream.
+
+## Build, Test, and Development Commands
+- Initialize dependencies: `git submodule update --init`.
+- Autotools flow: `autoreconf -i && ./configure --disable-dependency-tracking [flags] && make -j"$(nproc)" && make -j"$(nproc)" check`.
+- Library-only build: add `--enable-lib-only` to `./configure` to skip examples.
+- CMake flow: `cmake -B build -DENABLE_WERROR=ON [flags] && cmake --build build && cmake --build build --target check`.
+- Interop pytest suite: `pytest -v examples/tests` (filter with `-k`, for example `-k 'quictls-wolfssl'`).
+- Format sources: `make clang-format`.
+
+## Coding Style & Naming Conventions
+- Follow `.clang-format` exactly: 2-space indent, 80-column limit, no tabs.
+- Keep core protocol logic in `lib/`; TLS/provider integration belongs in `crypto/<backend>/`.
+- Use existing naming patterns: `ngtcp2_<module>.c/.h` and `ngtcp2_<module>_test.c/.h`.
+- Prefer small, focused patches; separate refactors from behavior changes.
+
+## Testing Guidelines
+- Add or update `tests/ngtcp2_*_test.c` for any library behavior change.
+- Run at least one local full pass: `make check` (autotools) or `cmake --build build --target check` (CMake).
+- For client/server, transport, or TLS changes, run `pytest -v examples/tests`.
+- There is no fixed coverage percentage target; coverage is enforced by meaningful regression tests across C tests and/or pytest interop tests.
+
+## Commit & Pull Request Guidelines
+- Follow recent history: concise, imperative subject lines, often with a scope prefix (examples: `ksl: ...`, `tests: ...`, `examples: ...`, `doc: ...`, `Bump ...`).
+- Keep commits logically grouped and buildable; avoid mixing unrelated subsystems.
+- PRs should state motivation, key design choices, linked issue (if applicable), and exact commands used to validate.
+- If behavior or build flags change, update `README.rst` and relevant docs in `doc/source/`.
+
+## Security & Configuration Tips
+- Follow `SECURITY.md` for vulnerability reporting.
+- Never commit certificates, keys, or local config secrets.
+- For local integration runs, generate temporary certs with `ci/gen-certificate.sh`.
